# BusyBox inittab for the custom_riscv board.
#
# The format is  <tty>:<runlevel>:<action>:<command>  and BusyBox ignores the
# runlevel field entirely. An empty tty field means /dev/console, which is the
# only terminal this machine has.
#
# There is deliberately no getty and no login here. getty exists to reset a
# terminal's line discipline and hand off to /bin/login, and login exists to
# check a password; on a board whose only console is a UART soldered to a USB
# bridge, both are ceremony that can only fail. The leading dash on the shell
# makes it a login shell, so it reads /etc/profile.
#
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# respawn, not once: leaving the shell gives you a new one instead of a dead
# machine that still has to be power-cycled.
::respawn:-/bin/sh

::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
::shutdown:/bin/sync
